1
00:00:31,780 --> 00:00:33,060
(A restaurant in Beijing)

2
00:00:33,480 --> 00:00:35,120
(Previously)
You can pick one guy

3
00:00:35,120 --> 00:00:37,120
to ride back with you.

4
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:38,120
Sent.

5
00:00:38,360 --> 00:00:39,880
Guess you're riding back with me.

6
00:00:39,880 --> 00:00:41,040
No problem.

7
00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:43,600
Sha Yue'er saw it all and heard it too.

8
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:44,600
I'm kinda...

9
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:45,440
upset.

10
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:46,920
Why'd he suddenly turn away?

11
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:48,680
First big date.

12
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:50,800
Liang Xiaoyu gets to pick

13
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:51,520
a one-on-one date.

14
00:00:51,520 --> 00:00:54,080
This season, one guy and one girl

15
00:00:54,080 --> 00:00:55,240
will each earn

16
00:00:55,240 --> 00:00:56,720
The Courageous first-date privilege.

17
00:00:57,820 --> 00:00:59,180
(Sun Qimeng picks Zhao Xilun)
Thanks.

18
00:00:59,360 --> 00:01:00,240
What a move!

19
00:01:00,440 --> 00:01:01,200
For me?

20
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:02,300
(Zhao Xilun picks Sha Yue'er)
Yeah, for you.

21
00:01:02,680 --> 00:01:05,320
Love favors the bold.

22
00:01:05,980 --> 00:01:07,180
(Date Day)

23
00:01:07,360 --> 00:01:08,520
Hello.

24
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:09,800
Let's trade, then.

25
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:10,400
You brought one too?

26
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:10,840
Yeah.

27
00:01:11,040 --> 00:01:12,600
Why'd you pick me?

28
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:13,760
I wanted to see you.

29
00:01:13,780 --> 00:01:15,180
(I wanted to see you)

30
00:01:16,600 --> 00:01:17,920
I'll study how they do this,
frame by frame.

31
00:01:18,440 --> 00:01:19,280
Let me get a little closer.

32
00:01:20,560 --> 00:01:21,080
Look at them.

33
00:01:21,080 --> 00:01:22,440
All that space...

34
00:01:22,440 --> 00:01:23,440
And they're whispering.

35
00:01:23,560 --> 00:01:24,800
It represents

36
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:26,480
always following the sun.

37
00:01:26,480 --> 00:01:27,240
(Always following the sun)

38
00:01:27,240 --> 00:01:28,920
He seems so quiet,

39
00:01:28,920 --> 00:01:30,480
but he's really smooth.

40
00:01:30,680 --> 00:01:31,600
You can take my hand.

41
00:01:31,720 --> 00:01:33,000
When we get back,

42
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:34,720
I'll say I need

43
00:01:34,720 --> 00:01:35,720
my trusty left hand.

44
00:01:37,240 --> 00:01:39,080
Your hands save lives.

45
00:01:39,080 --> 00:01:41,740
(Your hands save lives)

46
00:01:41,760 --> 00:01:42,910
(Mine are for hunting)
Mine are for hunting.

47
00:01:42,920 --> 00:01:43,680
Okay, I ship it.

48
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:44,680
Hunting hands.

49
00:01:47,220 --> 00:01:48,580
♪Don't stay trapped inside your room♪

50
00:01:48,580 --> 00:01:49,980
♪Outside the window,
the rain has cleared♪

51
00:01:49,980 --> 00:01:51,260
♪Set reality aside♪

52
00:01:51,260 --> 00:01:52,580
♪Follow your heart♪

53
00:01:52,580 --> 00:01:53,940
♪What you've been longing
for is right ahead♪

54
00:01:53,940 --> 00:01:55,420
♪Don't act like you didn't see it♪

55
00:01:55,420 --> 00:01:58,300
♪Just be a little braver♪

56
00:01:58,300 --> 00:02:01,060
♪Come closer, come closer♪

57
00:02:01,060 --> 00:02:04,140
♪There's a little spark
shining in your eyes♪

58
00:02:04,420 --> 00:02:06,260
♪That's the signal
of a heart coming alive♪

59
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:09,980
♪That's the signal
of a heart coming alive♪

60
00:02:09,980 --> 00:02:14,060
=Heart Signal (China Version) S9=

61
00:02:21,440 --> 00:02:22,840
The Courageous date.

62
00:02:24,180 --> 00:02:24,980
(Checks the time)

63
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:25,880
I can't wait.

64
00:02:25,880 --> 00:02:26,800
Me neither.

65
00:02:31,120 --> 00:02:32,800
There she is.

66
00:02:38,880 --> 00:02:40,240
She looks gorgeous.

67
00:02:40,240 --> 00:02:41,680
So pretty.

68
00:02:44,180 --> 00:02:45,020
(Deep breath)

69
00:02:45,040 --> 00:02:46,720
He's so nervous.

70
00:02:47,220 --> 00:02:48,780
(Clenches hands)

71
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:50,240
He's so nervous.

72
00:02:52,560 --> 00:02:53,480
Hello!

73
00:02:54,600 --> 00:02:56,040
So pretty.

74
00:02:58,920 --> 00:03:00,160
You're here.

75
00:03:00,160 --> 00:03:01,280
Have you eaten?

76
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:02,720
Just a little.

77
00:03:03,280 --> 00:03:04,560
Perfect. I...

78
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:05,360
You brought something?

79
00:03:05,640 --> 00:03:06,440
What's this?

80
00:03:06,840 --> 00:03:07,800
A low-sugar dessert.

81
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:12,040
And

82
00:03:12,040 --> 00:03:13,640
it has blueberries for inflammation.

83
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:17,120
Am I inflamed?

84
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:17,840
No.

85
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:18,560
It's just...

86
00:03:21,360 --> 00:03:22,440
I thought you might be tired.

87
00:03:22,440 --> 00:03:23,360
Just in case.

88
00:03:23,360 --> 00:03:23,600
You know.

89
00:03:23,600 --> 00:03:24,200
Thanks.

90
00:03:24,320 --> 00:03:25,280
So thoughtful.

91
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:27,800
Know what we're doing today?

92
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:28,280
Nope.

93
00:03:28,280 --> 00:03:28,760
What are we doing?

94
00:03:28,760 --> 00:03:29,360
Take a guess.

95
00:03:29,820 --> 00:03:31,340
(Laughs)

96
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:32,280
What is it?

97
00:03:33,400 --> 00:03:34,440
Let me guess.

98
00:03:34,940 --> 00:03:36,140
(Spots it)

99
00:03:37,440 --> 00:03:38,720
Slime?

100
00:03:39,600 --> 00:03:41,000
Oh, slime.

101
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:42,760
Let's go.

102
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:43,600
Let's go.

103
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:45,140
(Excited)

104
00:03:45,160 --> 00:03:46,800
Look how happy he is.

105
00:03:48,760 --> 00:03:49,960
He can't stop smiling.

106
00:03:50,320 --> 00:03:51,320
You haven't done this before, right?

107
00:03:51,320 --> 00:03:53,200
Not since you were little?

108
00:03:53,320 --> 00:03:54,040
Nope.

109
00:03:54,740 --> 00:03:56,740
(Slime Workshop)

110
00:03:56,760 --> 00:03:57,960
It's a DIY workshop.

111
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:00,840
Making slime.

112
00:04:01,480 --> 00:04:02,880
A little stress reliever.

113
00:04:02,880 --> 00:04:03,800
Squish it!

114
00:04:05,240 --> 00:04:06,040
(Offers her tea)
Thanks.

115
00:04:06,040 --> 00:04:06,880
Of course.

116
00:04:07,120 --> 00:04:08,280
So attentive.

117
00:04:08,440 --> 00:04:10,040
Have a seat.

118
00:04:16,700 --> 00:04:17,420
(Fumbles)

119
00:04:17,760 --> 00:04:19,400
Still a little nervous.

120
00:04:19,720 --> 00:04:20,800
You didn't expect this, huh?

121
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:22,280
(Keeps sipping tea)
Not at all.

122
00:04:22,280 --> 00:04:24,120
I thought we'd do something active.

123
00:04:24,120 --> 00:04:24,960
Is this...

124
00:04:25,440 --> 00:04:28,400
I never would've guessed this.

125
00:04:29,280 --> 00:04:30,280
Yeah.

126
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:31,920
I find it really relaxing.

127
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:34,200
And you can squish it at home.

128
00:04:34,200 --> 00:04:35,200
It smells nice too.

129
00:04:35,440 --> 00:04:36,480
I like nice scents.

130
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:38,920
So do I.

131
00:04:40,840 --> 00:04:42,920
Let's pick our colors first.

132
00:04:43,360 --> 00:04:45,040
What color do you want?

133
00:04:45,280 --> 00:04:46,080
Maybe blue.

134
00:04:46,840 --> 00:04:47,640
This one.

135
00:04:51,080 --> 00:04:51,680
That's so blue.

136
00:04:52,640 --> 00:04:53,680
Yours is so red.

137
00:04:55,520 --> 00:04:56,320
Next,

138
00:04:56,320 --> 00:04:58,280
this helps it set.

139
00:04:58,280 --> 00:04:59,080
Add a little more.

140
00:04:59,080 --> 00:05:00,640
I used too little. It got sticky.

141
00:05:01,800 --> 00:05:02,760
Let me do it.

142
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:03,720
Take a break.

143
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:04,880
I'm good.

144
00:05:06,760 --> 00:05:07,720
Look.

145
00:05:09,040 --> 00:05:10,160
This is so fun.

146
00:05:11,480 --> 00:05:13,160
Such a fun vibe.

147
00:05:13,160 --> 00:05:13,840
Yeah.

148
00:05:20,440 --> 00:05:22,240
Did you like this stuff as a kid?

149
00:05:22,260 --> 00:05:23,780
(Starts a conversation)

150
00:05:24,400 --> 00:05:25,880
Let me think.

151
00:05:25,880 --> 00:05:27,470
Yeah, definitely as a kid.

152
00:05:29,320 --> 00:05:29,920
When I was little...

153
00:05:29,920 --> 00:05:31,080
You know,

154
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:33,120
when you'd go grocery shopping
with your parents

155
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:34,280
and see those bins of rice?

156
00:05:34,280 --> 00:05:36,200
Didn't you just want to stick
your hand in?

157
00:05:36,720 --> 00:05:37,880
Totally.

158
00:05:37,880 --> 00:05:38,680
It's so fun.

159
00:05:38,960 --> 00:05:39,720
Right?

160
00:05:40,320 --> 00:05:41,800
But now that seems...

161
00:05:41,800 --> 00:05:42,400
Kind of...

162
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:43,120
Wrong.

163
00:05:43,120 --> 00:05:43,680
Yeah.

164
00:05:43,680 --> 00:05:44,200
True.

165
00:05:45,880 --> 00:05:46,600
I can't exactly

166
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:47,920
take you to a grocery store

167
00:05:47,920 --> 00:05:48,760
(Joking)
to play with the rice.

168
00:05:49,640 --> 00:05:50,600
Yeah, maybe not.

169
00:05:51,490 --> 00:05:52,320
That's hilarious.

170
00:05:58,960 --> 00:06:00,480
Did you ever wish

171
00:06:00,480 --> 00:06:01,640
you had superpowers or something?

172
00:06:02,040 --> 00:06:03,200
That's so random.

173
00:06:03,200 --> 00:06:03,960
All the time.

174
00:06:03,960 --> 00:06:05,240
Especially as a kid.

175
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:06,720
I really wanted clones.

176
00:06:07,160 --> 00:06:08,240
Clones?

177
00:06:08,240 --> 00:06:09,560
I have so much I want to do.

178
00:06:09,560 --> 00:06:10,400
I can't do it all myself.

179
00:06:11,200 --> 00:06:13,240
I'd teleport and stop time.

180
00:06:13,440 --> 00:06:14,520
I'd love that too.

181
00:06:16,280 --> 00:06:18,080
I just feel

182
00:06:18,080 --> 00:06:19,120
like there's never enough time.

183
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:20,600
If you could teleport,

184
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:21,520
you'd actually

185
00:06:21,520 --> 00:06:22,840
save so much time.

186
00:06:23,120 --> 00:06:24,060
(Agrees)
Yeah.

187
00:06:24,060 --> 00:06:24,960
Exactly.

188
00:06:24,960 --> 00:06:26,200
Kind of scary, though.

189
00:06:26,200 --> 00:06:27,240
Yeah.

190
00:06:27,440 --> 00:06:29,000
They really think alike.

191
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:30,920
I think Zhao Xilun's approach

192
00:06:30,920 --> 00:06:31,960
helps you relax,

193
00:06:31,960 --> 00:06:32,400
you know?

194
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:32,880
Then being together

195
00:06:32,880 --> 00:06:34,440
just feels a lot more comfortable.

196
00:06:34,720 --> 00:06:36,840
I even make up rules for myself.

197
00:06:36,840 --> 00:06:37,440
Like,

198
00:06:37,440 --> 00:06:38,200
I'd have to...

199
00:06:38,200 --> 00:06:38,960
For example,

200
00:06:38,960 --> 00:06:39,600
I could only

201
00:06:39,600 --> 00:06:40,720
stop time for a bit each day.

202
00:06:41,200 --> 00:06:41,960
Okay.

203
00:06:41,960 --> 00:06:42,440
Yeah.

204
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:47,840
I really want to stop time today.

205
00:06:48,060 --> 00:06:49,220
(I really want to stop time today)

206
00:06:51,560 --> 00:06:53,000
That was good.

207
00:06:53,240 --> 00:06:54,920
I really want to stop time today.

208
00:06:54,920 --> 00:06:55,900
(I really want to stop time today)

209
00:07:02,880 --> 00:07:03,800
There's definitely

210
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:05,720
a spark between them now.

211
00:07:05,720 --> 00:07:06,920
Nice.

212
00:07:12,880 --> 00:07:13,840
Let me smell yours.

213
00:07:13,840 --> 00:07:14,400
Go ahead.

214
00:07:16,480 --> 00:07:17,320
Yours smells so good.

215
00:07:17,860 --> 00:07:18,700
(Happy)

216
00:07:18,880 --> 00:07:19,680
Smell this one.

217
00:07:25,640 --> 00:07:26,280
It smells like roses.

218
00:07:26,840 --> 00:07:27,600
I like it.

219
00:07:28,940 --> 00:07:30,500
(Shy)

220
00:07:34,440 --> 00:07:35,600
I'm going to take my jacket off.

221
00:07:35,600 --> 00:07:36,280
Honestly...

222
00:07:37,360 --> 00:07:39,040
You can tell he's nervous.

223
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:39,680
Yeah.

224
00:07:47,880 --> 00:07:48,440
Do you know

225
00:07:48,440 --> 00:07:49,680
my first impression of you?

226
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:52,840
The first time I saw you,

227
00:07:52,840 --> 00:07:53,960
your ears really...

228
00:07:54,440 --> 00:07:55,480
Stick out, right?

229
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:56,040
Yeah, they stick out.

230
00:07:56,040 --> 00:07:56,440
Yeah.

231
00:07:56,680 --> 00:07:58,680
So you really stood out to me.

232
00:07:58,680 --> 00:08:00,180
(You really stood out to me)

233
00:08:05,880 --> 00:08:06,520
Have you noticed?

234
00:08:06,520 --> 00:08:07,960
You actually...

235
00:08:08,120 --> 00:08:09,520
can't see my ears

236
00:08:09,520 --> 00:08:10,160
from the front.

237
00:08:11,400 --> 00:08:12,960
Bet side-sleeping is comfy.

238
00:08:13,240 --> 00:08:14,840
Very comfy.

239
00:08:16,160 --> 00:08:17,400
Smooth save.

240
00:08:17,720 --> 00:08:19,280
What a way to look at it.

241
00:08:21,560 --> 00:08:22,560
What about you?

242
00:08:22,560 --> 00:08:23,440
When we first met,

243
00:08:23,440 --> 00:08:24,640
what did you think of me?

244
00:08:24,640 --> 00:08:25,360
My impression

245
00:08:25,360 --> 00:08:26,320
was you didn't remember me.

246
00:08:26,980 --> 00:08:28,740
(Freezes)

247
00:08:28,760 --> 00:08:29,880
He froze.

248
00:08:30,360 --> 00:08:31,160
You...

249
00:08:31,720 --> 00:08:33,320
That's not a great impression.

250
00:08:36,520 --> 00:08:37,920
Do you actually remember me?

251
00:08:39,040 --> 00:08:40,400
I really do.

252
00:08:48,240 --> 00:08:49,520
I really do.

253
00:08:50,120 --> 00:08:51,760
How could I forget?

254
00:08:53,880 --> 00:08:54,960
Now I can't even tell

255
00:08:54,960 --> 00:08:55,600
when you're being honest

256
00:08:55,600 --> 00:08:56,800
and when you're not.

257
00:08:58,640 --> 00:08:59,640
Usually,

258
00:08:59,640 --> 00:09:01,640
when I look at you like this,

259
00:09:01,640 --> 00:09:03,160
right into your eyes...

260
00:09:07,380 --> 00:09:09,740
(Eye contact)

261
00:09:10,520 --> 00:09:11,320
I'm telling the truth.

262
00:09:11,320 --> 00:09:12,120
Okay.

263
00:09:19,400 --> 00:09:20,720
Mine's a little runny.

264
00:09:22,800 --> 00:09:24,440
Want me to knead it for you?

265
00:09:25,320 --> 00:09:25,840
Sure.

266
00:09:25,840 --> 00:09:27,280
I don't want to get you all sticky.

267
00:09:30,480 --> 00:09:31,600
Yours is really sticky.

268
00:09:32,640 --> 00:09:34,240
Why's your watch on your right wrist?

269
00:09:34,240 --> 00:09:35,000
I'm left-handed.

270
00:09:36,440 --> 00:09:37,600
You're a lefty?

271
00:09:37,600 --> 00:09:38,120
Yeah,

272
00:09:38,120 --> 00:09:39,320
so I think

273
00:09:39,320 --> 00:09:40,640
I'm pretty good

274
00:09:40,640 --> 00:09:41,400
at creative thinking.

275
00:09:42,200 --> 00:09:43,000
Me too.

276
00:09:43,200 --> 00:09:44,600
I can tell.

277
00:09:44,600 --> 00:09:45,640
But your major

278
00:09:45,640 --> 00:09:46,480
doesn't really

279
00:09:46,480 --> 00:09:47,960
call for much creativity, right?

280
00:09:54,560 --> 00:09:55,640
I kind of regret

281
00:09:55,640 --> 00:09:57,480
not choosing a STEM major.

282
00:09:59,120 --> 00:09:59,960
Yeah, we talked about that.

283
00:09:59,960 --> 00:10:01,640
You said you really liked physics.

284
00:10:03,040 --> 00:10:04,240
I just felt like...

285
00:10:05,520 --> 00:10:07,120
I wasn't naturally gifted.

286
00:10:11,160 --> 00:10:13,320
I got my grades by grinding.

287
00:10:14,400 --> 00:10:17,240
It never came easily to me.

288
00:10:22,920 --> 00:10:24,560
I think

289
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:25,680
you're selling yourself short.

290
00:10:27,920 --> 00:10:29,280
Depends what you want to do.

291
00:10:29,840 --> 00:10:31,400
For pure theory,

292
00:10:31,400 --> 00:10:33,200
you need inspiration and talent.

293
00:10:33,200 --> 00:10:34,880
Take Gauss.

294
00:10:34,880 --> 00:10:36,320
He was already

295
00:10:36,320 --> 00:10:37,320
a mathematician as a teenager.

296
00:10:37,320 --> 00:10:37,840
Right.

297
00:10:38,080 --> 00:10:39,120
By that standard,

298
00:10:39,120 --> 00:10:40,040
honestly,

299
00:10:40,040 --> 00:10:41,960
most people in my major aren't gifted.

300
00:10:41,960 --> 00:10:43,360
I'm definitely not.

301
00:10:43,720 --> 00:10:44,880
He's good at reassuring her.

302
00:10:46,320 --> 00:10:48,200
They've been into it
since they were kids

303
00:10:48,200 --> 00:10:49,200
and just kept at it.

304
00:10:49,560 --> 00:10:50,600
Exactly.

305
00:10:51,760 --> 00:10:54,000
So when you chose your major,

306
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:55,600
did you think about careers?

307
00:10:57,760 --> 00:10:59,160
I did.

308
00:10:59,160 --> 00:11:01,280
I considered a few paths.

309
00:11:01,680 --> 00:11:02,680
With this major,

310
00:11:02,680 --> 00:11:04,680
I could work
for an international organization

311
00:11:04,880 --> 00:11:08,080
or get a master's in law.

312
00:11:08,920 --> 00:11:10,040
When it comes to law,

313
00:11:10,040 --> 00:11:11,440
I honestly don't know much about it.

314
00:11:11,440 --> 00:11:12,560
But AI is moving so fast,

315
00:11:12,560 --> 00:11:14,120
it could reshape the whole field

316
00:11:14,720 --> 00:11:17,360
and change how people work.

317
00:11:18,840 --> 00:11:20,400
I love chatting with AI.

318
00:11:21,840 --> 00:11:23,200
Do I sound like AI?

319
00:11:23,200 --> 00:11:24,760
I always think I do.

320
00:11:25,180 --> 00:11:26,620
(Curious)

321
00:11:27,400 --> 00:11:28,640
Not really.

322
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:29,600
Really?

323
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:31,160
Understood.

324
00:11:31,160 --> 00:11:33,360
I'll give you a direct response.

325
00:11:34,600 --> 00:11:36,080
Oh my God!

326
00:11:36,080 --> 00:11:37,560
I won't say who you sound like.

327
00:11:38,280 --> 00:11:40,080
I sound like someone specific?

328
00:11:40,080 --> 00:11:41,840
Or a specific AI?

329
00:11:42,440 --> 00:11:43,760
Yeah, a specific AI.

330
00:11:46,240 --> 00:11:47,800
What about your career?

331
00:11:47,800 --> 00:11:48,800
Any goals for the future?

332
00:11:50,920 --> 00:11:52,320
I don't really dare

333
00:11:52,320 --> 00:11:53,320
set expectations.

334
00:11:53,320 --> 00:11:53,920
Because

335
00:11:54,280 --> 00:11:56,160
at our age,

336
00:11:56,680 --> 00:11:58,760
so much is out of our control.

337
00:11:58,760 --> 00:12:00,160
You just have to try things.

338
00:12:00,360 --> 00:12:00,920
Like,

339
00:12:01,240 --> 00:12:02,680
sometimes

340
00:12:02,680 --> 00:12:03,960
you don't even know

341
00:12:03,960 --> 00:12:04,880
what'll happen next week.

342
00:12:05,240 --> 00:12:06,360
Things change so fast.

343
00:12:07,480 --> 00:12:07,760
Yeah.

344
00:12:07,760 --> 00:12:08,720
Yesterday, I had no idea

345
00:12:08,720 --> 00:12:09,880
what today would bring.

346
00:12:15,280 --> 00:12:16,200
Sometimes ideas

347
00:12:16,200 --> 00:12:17,600
just come out of nowhere.

348
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:20,000
We can't control how things change.

349
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:20,880
All we can do

350
00:12:20,880 --> 00:12:22,000
is keep growing

351
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:23,360
and give ourselves more options.

352
00:12:24,120 --> 00:12:25,760
He always knows what to say.

353
00:12:26,650 --> 00:12:27,280
And

354
00:12:27,280 --> 00:12:28,720
for Sha Yue'er,

355
00:12:28,720 --> 00:12:29,360
it probably hits

356
00:12:29,360 --> 00:12:30,560
a little differently.

357
00:12:38,200 --> 00:12:39,680
Why did you want

358
00:12:39,680 --> 00:12:41,840
to go for the Courageous?

359
00:12:45,480 --> 00:12:46,440
I figured

360
00:12:47,440 --> 00:12:48,000
if I didn't go for it,

361
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:49,240
someone else definitely would.

362
00:12:58,440 --> 00:12:59,440
She was captivated.

363
00:12:59,740 --> 00:13:00,630
She fell for it.

364
00:13:01,320 --> 00:13:03,240
Yeah, so I thought,

365
00:13:03,390 --> 00:13:04,600
why not be brave for once?

366
00:13:08,560 --> 00:13:09,080
Cause

367
00:13:09,080 --> 00:13:10,000
I feel like

368
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:11,800
courage is something

369
00:13:11,800 --> 00:13:13,760
I really lack.

370
00:13:14,360 --> 00:13:15,960
But you were pretty brave yesterday.

371
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:18,920
You mean when we went...

372
00:13:18,920 --> 00:13:20,360
No, I mean

373
00:13:20,360 --> 00:13:22,120
